WEBVTT

00:04.470 --> 00:08.510
How is the operation coming along, Vamp?

00:08.510 --> 00:10.030
We're currently—

00:10.030 --> 00:12.210
What are you doing, grandpa?

00:12.210 --> 00:13.650
Come on, Ma,

00:13.650 --> 00:15.710
didn't I tell you not to come in?

01:47.650 --> 01:51.610
Vamp sent you some kind of package.

01:52.120 --> 01:55.150
I bet they sent us something weird again.

01:55.150 --> 01:57.060
It's pretty big.

01:57.060 --> 01:58.460
I wonder what it is.

01:59.550 --> 02:00.320
What the hell is this?

02:04.250 --> 02:07.270
Why, how are you Kayoko?

02:07.270 --> 02:09.250
Thank goodness they arrived.

02:09.250 --> 02:10.590
Yes.

02:10.590 --> 02:13.160
I thought it'd be a good idea to share some with Mr. Red as well.

02:13.160 --> 02:14.760
That's so thoughtful of you, thank—

02:14.760 --> 02:15.890
Let me talk to him real quick.

02:15.890 --> 02:16.810
What are you—

02:16.810 --> 02:18.100
Hey punk!

02:18.100 --> 02:19.460
H-Hello, Mr. Red.

02:19.460 --> 02:21.860
What the hell is this?

02:21.860 --> 02:23.510
Were you surprised?

02:23.510 --> 02:25.630
It was our youngins' idea;

02:25.630 --> 02:29.230
we figured we'd start selling these as a way of raising funds for our operations.

02:29.230 --> 02:32.650
What the hell kind of evil organization sells sausages?

02:32.650 --> 02:34.170
Don't worry.

02:34.170 --> 02:37.080
We have a vendor's license and everything.

02:37.710 --> 02:40.420
I was also skeptical about it myself,

02:40.420 --> 02:43.740
but I thought nothing bad could come out of actually listening to the youngins' opinions—

02:43.740 --> 02:46.220
You're missing the point again.

02:46.220 --> 02:49.320
You better not have put anything weird inside.

02:49.320 --> 02:50.510
Of course not!

02:50.510 --> 02:53.760
Our sausages are made of 100% fish!

02:53.760 --> 02:56.690
We haven't used any artificial colorings either.

02:56.690 --> 02:57.610
Oh yeah?

02:57.610 --> 02:59.650
You can eat it raw,

02:59.650 --> 03:02.600
or even slice it up and use it in fried rice too.

03:02.600 --> 03:04.330
I'm hanging up.

03:04.890 --> 03:06.490
Usa!

03:06.490 --> 03:08.530
I see you've found it.

03:08.530 --> 03:13.010
Each box comes with a plastic figurine of one of our monsters.

03:13.010 --> 03:14.430
They're really well-made.

03:14.430 --> 03:16.040
You're pretty lucky.

03:16.040 --> 03:18.630
I hear the Usakotsu figurines are pretty rare.

03:18.630 --> 03:20.700
Really? Awesome.

03:20.700 --> 03:23.160
There's quite a few of them,

03:23.160 --> 03:24.960
so good luck collecting—

03:27.000 --> 03:30.530
I don't think Mr. Red likes sausages all that much.

03:30.530 --> 03:35.260
These sausages are really high quality, I'll give you that.

03:35.260 --> 03:37.880
We couldn't sell any, though.

03:37.880 --> 03:40.360
What did we do wrong?

03:40.360 --> 03:42.980
Our marketing strategy was flawless.

03:42.980 --> 03:46.970
But at least I won't have to buy groceries for a while now.

03:46.970 --> 03:49.000
I'm tired of sausages!

03:49.000 --> 03:51.270
No one likes a picky eater.

03:51.270 --> 03:53.760
It's all because we screwed up on the distribution part.

03:53.760 --> 03:56.450
If only we had been able to advertise these on a large scale—

03:56.450 --> 03:59.380
It's all because you didn't plan this out like you should have, dumbass.

03:59.380 --> 04:00.030
Shut up!

04:00.030 --> 04:02.960
At least my idea became commercialized, unlike your stupid "Florsheim Cup Noodles" idea.

04:02.960 --> 04:04.900
You just had to open old wounds didn't you?

04:04.900 --> 04:07.410
Why don't <i>you </i> try coming up with something better, then?

04:08.460 --> 04:10.100
Come on, you guys.

04:10.100 --> 04:11.770
Stop it.

04:11.770 --> 04:13.060
Sorry to have kept you waiting.

04:13.060 --> 04:16.180
We made some sausage casserole.

04:22.140 --> 04:25.530
These sausages are better than I thought.

04:25.530 --> 04:27.450
Oh geez, not another Geirus again.

04:36.150 --> 04:38.800
General Hengel of Florsheim's West Tokyo Division.

04:38.800 --> 04:41.810
He is also known as the "Master of Scissors."

04:41.810 --> 04:43.880
His scissors, which are said to cut as well as the devil himself,

04:43.880 --> 04:45.890
are constantly on the look out for something to cut!

04:45.890 --> 04:47.950
Oh my.

04:47.950 --> 04:49.420
Looks like we've got tangled up.

04:49.420 --> 04:51.190
I'm so sorry.

04:51.650 --> 04:53.930
Do you wish for me to cut it?

04:54.330 --> 04:56.280
Oh no, we can untangle it.

04:56.280 --> 05:00.320
My scissors can even cut through diamond.

05:00.320 --> 05:01.990
There's no need to be polite!

05:01.990 --> 05:03.760
We're fine, really.

05:03.760 --> 05:06.830
He looks like he's dying to cut it.

05:07.540 --> 05:09.420
In that case, please go ahead.

05:15.490 --> 05:18.100
Good morning, you guys.

05:18.250 --> 05:21.290
I'd like to introduce you guys to someone new today.

05:21.290 --> 05:25.280
This is Logis, and he'll be joining our division straight out of college.

05:24.980 --> 05:28.190
Florsheim Monster
Logis (Newbie)

05:25.280 --> 05:27.860
He just graduated college this spring.

05:27.860 --> 05:29.470
What up.

05:30.260 --> 05:32.210
Let's see...

05:32.210 --> 05:36.260
Could you mentor him and show how
we do things around here, Geddon?

05:36.260 --> 05:37.940
M-Me?

05:37.940 --> 05:39.710
That's quite a responsibility, Geddon.

05:39.710 --> 05:40.930
A mentor?

05:40.930 --> 05:43.690
Well then, I guess we'll see you around tomorrow.

05:43.690 --> 05:45.610
Nice to meet you.

05:45.610 --> 05:47.660
Oh, yeah.

05:50.950 --> 05:52.890
Oh man.

05:52.890 --> 05:54.600
Me, a mentor?

05:54.600 --> 05:57.550
I would have become an office worker if I knew this would happen.

05:57.550 --> 06:00.050
But I don't want to disappoint Master Vamp either.

06:00.050 --> 06:01.630
What am I supposed to mentor him on?

06:01.630 --> 06:04.790
I guess I should start with everyday basics.

06:06.060 --> 06:09.900
All right. I'm going to try to write down everything I want to teach Logis.

06:10.080 --> 06:13.830
I guess there's quite a few, now  that I think about it.

06:15.540 --> 06:18.420
That's all for our morning rolecall.

06:18.420 --> 06:20.490
Let me explain it to you then.

06:20.490 --> 06:23.070
You see the quick sweeper over here?

06:23.070 --> 06:26.630
We usually do a quick cleanup after morning rolecall so use this to sweep the floor, okay?

06:26.840 --> 06:27.690
Okay.

06:27.690 --> 06:28.290
Are you listening?

06:28.290 --> 06:29.020
I am.

06:29.020 --> 06:30.690
What the, how did this sheet get so dirty?

06:30.690 --> 06:32.280
Who forgot to change this?

06:32.280 --> 06:36.160
World domination starts from getting little things like this done right.

06:36.160 --> 06:38.280
It's sad that a lot of people don't understand that nowadays.

06:38.280 --> 06:39.130
Hey Geddon?

06:39.130 --> 06:40.830
What's this Quick Riper thing again?

06:40.830 --> 06:42.290
It's called a Quick <i>Hiper</i>.

06:42.290 --> 06:43.540
No, <i>Wiper.</i>

06:43.540 --> 06:44.940
Do you have a girlfriend, Number Two?

06:44.940 --> 06:45.940
Yeah I do.

06:45.940 --> 06:46.600
Really?

06:46.600 --> 06:48.340
You have one too, don't you?

06:48.340 --> 06:49.510
You wanna go to a nightclub some time then?

06:49.510 --> 06:51.340
Wait a second, what?

06:51.340 --> 06:52.260
I said I <i>have </i> a girlfriend.

06:52.260 --> 06:54.280
So what? You can still go.

06:54.280 --> 06:55.560
So you think clubbing is a whole different thing then?

06:55.560 --> 06:58.450
I've got to get Logis to be friends with everyone,

06:58.450 --> 07:01.440
and to do that, I have to get to know him better first as his mentor.

07:01.440 --> 07:04.500
I guess the best way to do that would be to drink and pour our hearts out.

07:04.500 --> 07:05.890
All right!

07:05.890 --> 07:08.030
You got a minute, Logis?

07:08.030 --> 07:09.280
What is it?

07:09.280 --> 07:11.480
Do you wanna go out for a drink tonight?

07:11.480 --> 07:14.900
I'm supposed to meet someone today, sorry.

07:16.180 --> 07:17.450
Oh sorry.

07:17.450 --> 07:19.370
I guess I should have asked if you were free first.

07:19.370 --> 07:21.090
In that case why don't we go when you're free next—

07:21.090 --> 07:24.740
Sorry, I have to get this.

07:24.740 --> 07:26.250
Hello?

07:26.250 --> 07:28.520
Yeah it's me. Where you at?

07:28.520 --> 07:30.550
Yeah, it's hella hot.

07:31.050 --> 07:33.940
No way, shut up, dumbass.

07:37.370 --> 07:39.140
What is this?

07:39.140 --> 07:41.280
It's exactly what it says it is.

07:41.280 --> 07:43.910
This is a worksheet from the study group that we're running.

07:43.910 --> 07:46.670
You should fill one out and turn it in tomorrow too, Logis.

07:46.670 --> 07:47.940
For reals?

07:47.940 --> 07:50.540
This really isn't my thing.

07:50.540 --> 07:53.230
Master Vamp didn't say I had to do this, right?

07:54.140 --> 07:56.020
It doesn't matter if it isn't your thing.

07:56.020 --> 07:56.770
All the other monsters are doing this too.

07:56.770 --> 07:59.870
Why can't I just think up something threatening when I meet Red

07:59.870 --> 08:02.190
and just say it on the spot instead?

08:02.190 --> 08:04.900
You might get nervous and screw up that way.

08:04.900 --> 08:06.540
Even Midogelg the other time couldn't—

08:06.540 --> 08:08.810
The others have their own ways,

08:08.810 --> 08:11.110
just like I have my own.

08:13.530 --> 08:16.120
So how are things going with Logis?

08:16.120 --> 08:18.500
Well, what can I say...

08:18.500 --> 08:20.780
He's from a different generation.

08:20.780 --> 08:23.520
You can't be too nice to him.

08:23.520 --> 08:25.830
You have to say what needs to be said, sometimes.

08:26.550 --> 08:27.380
Yes, sir.

08:37.590 --> 08:40.050
If I'm going to get a dog...

08:40.320 --> 08:42.510
then I better get some toys for him too.

08:45.200 --> 08:47.910
How the hell are you late for two days straight?

08:47.910 --> 08:51.010
You're making me look bad as your mentor.

08:51.010 --> 08:51.930
Sorry.

08:51.930 --> 08:53.540
I wanted to say this earlier,

08:53.540 --> 08:55.360
but you shouldn't chew gum when others are talking to you.

08:55.360 --> 08:56.960
It's really rude, you know.

08:56.960 --> 08:58.930
Sorry.

09:03.170 --> 09:05.420
Geez, when's he going to realize he's not a student anymore?

09:05.420 --> 09:07.900
He may be handsome and may have come out of a good college,

09:07.900 --> 09:10.130
but he still doesn't know how to act like a member of society.

09:10.130 --> 09:13.870
I'll have to show him just how cruel society can be, as his mentor.

09:14.830 --> 09:16.460
I'm so tired.

09:16.460 --> 09:18.130
Hey Logis,

09:18.130 --> 09:19.240
What is it?

09:19.240 --> 09:21.140
So hey,

09:21.140 --> 09:24.670
I'm fighting Red tomorrow; want to come?

09:25.220 --> 09:26.450
I'm supposed to get tomorrow off—

09:26.450 --> 09:28.200
Just come with me!

09:28.200 --> 09:31.120
Just show up and watch me fight him!

09:31.120 --> 09:33.750
It's not like I'm asking you to fight too.

09:33.750 --> 09:35.310
Okay?

09:35.310 --> 09:36.440
Sure.

09:36.440 --> 09:37.680
All right.

09:37.680 --> 09:39.220
That was scary, man.

09:39.220 --> 09:40.330
Why's he all aggressive and shit?

09:40.330 --> 09:44.790
Watch me fight and try to see the error of your ways, Logis!

09:49.390 --> 09:51.810
I'm gonna go play some pachinko.

09:53.700 --> 09:54.970
There you are.

09:54.970 --> 09:58.420
I'm sorry I'm late.

09:58.980 --> 10:02.550
I went to a group date last night and ended up pulling an all-nighter.

10:02.550 --> 10:04.860
Was <i>that </i> Red?

10:04.860 --> 10:07.080
He looks hella dangerous, man.

10:07.080 --> 10:08.660
He's got one hell of an aura.

10:08.660 --> 10:10.700
It was all red and shit.

10:10.700 --> 10:13.490
Oh yeah, could you give this to Master Vamp for me?

10:13.490 --> 10:16.030
Come on already, Logi!

10:16.030 --> 10:18.330
My bad, I'm comin'.

10:18.780 --> 10:22.580
What are you all in a hurry for?

10:22.580 --> 10:23.820
Where do you wanna go?

10:24.010 --> 10:27.170
And that happened three years ago.

10:27.170 --> 10:28.540
That's too bad.

10:28.540 --> 10:31.100
I miss Geddon.

10:31.100 --> 10:34.100
So what does that awesome story...

10:34.100 --> 10:37.790
have anything to do with these awesome strawberries?

10:37.790 --> 10:38.390
Strawberries!

10:38.390 --> 10:40.130
Oh yeah, so,

10:40.130 --> 10:42.240
Geddon ended up quitting too,

10:42.240 --> 10:44.380
and decided to work at a strawberry farm instead.

10:44.380 --> 10:46.360
I was wondering where the story was going.

10:46.360 --> 10:47.990
That's awesome, but what happened next?

10:47.990 --> 10:50.460
So he sends us strawberries like this every year

10:50.460 --> 10:51.910
when the Tochiotohime Strawberries are in season.

10:51.910 --> 10:54.500
He was a really

10:54.500 --> 10:58.570
Why don't we all go on a strawberry hunt over to Geddon's farm, then?

10:58.570 --> 11:00.820
Yeah, let's go.

11:00.820 --> 11:02.200
We can have a reunion while we're at it.

11:02.200 --> 11:04.120
We should try to go before the rainy season.

11:04.120 --> 11:06.220
I'll ask Geddon when the best time to visit is.

11:06.220 --> 11:09.570
I hope they have tons of strawberries!

11:12.900 --> 11:14.740
Hey Geddon,

11:14.740 --> 11:17.910
lunch is ready, so...

11:17.910 --> 11:19.480
Okay.

11:19.480 --> 11:21.690
I'll be right there, Sachi.

11:26.060 --> 11:29.800
Daddy, Geddon's joining us too.

11:31.010 --> 11:34.990
I think it's about time I propose to you,

11:34.990 --> 11:36.700
Sachi.

11:38.210 --> 11:40.190
Dear Master Vamp,

11:40.190 --> 11:42.490
The sweet and sour strawberries

11:42.490 --> 11:44.630
are in full bloom again this year.
